{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:b16a0d497788384f","name":"Mandalorian Warrior Talent Tree","source":{"id":"source:reference-b16a0d497788384f","title":"Mandalorian Warrior Talent Tree","revision":27436,"timestamp":"2026-08-26T03:16:20Z","sha256":"fc44a6f5cbe77cc2518841f6751e0baf86a43d53fc8028981c50ce119dccaf4d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=27436","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Mandalorian%20Warrior%20Talent%20Tree&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-b16a0d497788384f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorians"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorians","referenceId":"reference:b7f4f8a44de3a6c8"}," are talented and ferocious warriors. Their skillful training, warrior culture, and advanced combat abilities make them formidable foes in any era. The following Talents are particularly suited to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"},".\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Armored Mandalorian"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," 13, ",{"tag":"b","children":["Mandalorian Glory"]},", Proficient with Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mandalorians wear armor constantly and learn to adjust to take an impact on the strongest section of their armor. You add your armor's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," bonus as an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus to your Elite Trooper ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," (with a maximum bonus equal to your base ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Trooper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Trooper","referenceId":"reference:02fa86cb25e21540"}," DR). Additionally, if ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," do not ignore the DR of the armor you are wearing (such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cortosis Weave/Phrik Alloy General Template"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cortosis_Weave/Phrik_Alloy_General_Template","referenceId":"reference:a2d70c9a2a420be5"},"), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," do not ignore your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Elite Trooper"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Elite_Trooper","referenceId":"reference:02fa86cb25e21540"}," Damage Reduction.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Mandalorian Advance"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Veteran Mandalorians know how to move on the battlefield. Once per encounter, on your turn, you can ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move","referenceId":"reference:6ecc3df6bffdd06c"}," up to your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Speed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Speed","referenceId":"reference:c372fee9b4566b85"}," as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Free Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Free_Action"}," before any other Action. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Mandalorian Ferocity"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," 13\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mandalorians can be ferocious fighters. Select one ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Group"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Group"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," you are proficient with. Once per encounter, when making more than one attack in a round, you can add one damage die to each successful hit with the selected ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Group"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Group"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"},". You can take this Talent more than once, selecting a different ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapon"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Group"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Group"}," each time.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Mandalorian Glory"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Above everything else, Mandalorians fight for glory in battle. Once per encounter, when you reduce an opponent's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," to 0, you gain a +5 attack bonus with your next attack roll during the same encounter.\n"]},"\n"]}}
